<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fernando Belaúnde Terry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/2002">2002</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fernando Belaúnde Terry was a Peruvian architect and politician, founder of the Popular Action party, who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1963 to 1968 and from 1980 to 1985. His first government, which promoted roads and settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a>, was overthrown by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-velasco-alvarado">Juan Velasco Alvarado</a>. Returning in 1980 as the military handed back power, he faced the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a> insurgency, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-nino">El Niño</a> of 1983 and economic crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fernando-belaunde-terry.jpg" alt="Fernando Belaúnde Terry" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 144155804@N02 (Flickr) · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fernando_Bela%C3%BAnde_Terry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
